course: dictionary
lesson: 4250
title: Graphite: the soft grey form of carbon
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You may meet the word graphite in science or in your pencil case. Read the words around it for clues. «Pencil "lead" is graphite, a kind of carbon, mixed with clay; it contains no lead metal.» The words "contains no lead metal" tell you that graphite is not the heavy metal lead, even though people often call the inside of a pencil "lead".
explain: Look at the other clues. Graphite is soft, grey and shiny, and it leaves marks on paper, so it is used in pencils. Swap your meaning into the sentence: "a pencil is made of soft carbon mixed with clay" still makes sense, so you have the right idea.
explain: One word can name a material that does different jobs. Graphite is used in batteries, as a lubricant and in sports gear like tennis rackets. In science, the clue is that graphite and diamond are both pure carbon, but their atoms are arranged differently, so they behave differently.
fact: Graphite is a soft, dark grey form of carbon.
fact: «Graphite» leaves marks on paper, which is why it is used in pencils.
fact: The "lead" in a pencil is graphite mixed with clay, and it contains no lead metal.
fact: Graphite is also used in batteries, as a lubricant, and in sports gear like tennis rackets.
fact: Diamond and graphite are both pure carbon, but their atoms are arranged differently: diamond is very hard, while graphite is soft and slippery.
exercise: «Pencil "lead" is graphite, a kind of carbon, mixed with clay; it contains no lead metal.» What does this tell you about graphite? | It is a type of paint | It is a heavy metal, just like lead | *It is a soft form of carbon, not the metal lead | It is a kind of wood
exercise: Graphite leaves marks on paper. Which object uses graphite to make its marks? | *A pencil | A paintbrush | A pen full of ink | A bar of soap
exercise: Which two things are both pure carbon, with their atoms arranged differently? | Graphite and lead metal | Lead and clay | Tennis racket and battery | *Diamond and graphite
test: Graphite is used in batteries and in sports gear. Which of these uses graphite? | *A tennis racket | A stone wall | A glass of water | A wooden ruler
test: «Diamond is very hard, but graphite is soft and slippery.» Why are they different, if both are pure carbon? | One has no carbon in it | *Their atoms are arranged differently | One is made by a machine and one is not | One is a metal and one is wood
exam: «Pencil "lead" is graphite, a kind of carbon.» Which statement is true? | Graphite is only used to make diamonds | Graphite is a type of wood | Pencil lead is the heavy metal lead | *Graphite is a soft, grey form of carbon
